  "description": "<p>The University of Western Australia (UWA) is a public research university situated in Perth, Western Australia. Founded in 1911, it is one of the most prestigious universities in <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/countries/study-in-australia/\">Australia</a>.</p><p>Recognised internationally for its exceptional learning, research and faculties, it is also one of the oldest universities in Australia. UWA holds a five-star rating for teaching quality, facilitating meaningful teaching, learning and research in the Good Universities Guide, so graduates from this acknowledged university have the best possible chance of future success.</p><h2>What is the University of Western Australia acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The University of Western Australia acceptance rate is 38%.</p> <p>UWA houses first-rate lecture theaters, laboratories and places of learning like the Reid and Science libraries that are packed with information for students to enjoy. Students can be assured of the quality of the facilities at this prestigious university, with sports facilities so students can stay active such as the UWA Sports Park. Other notable amenities include the UWA Aquatic Centre or the John de Laeter Centre for Mass Spectrometry.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>More than 25,000 students find a home on the main campus, with more than 4,000 international students coming from 100 countries to study here.</p><p>There are over 160 student clubs and societies to join, including Australiaâ€™s most active Student Guild for students who want to make their voice heard. UWA sport opportunities are surplus, with a fully kitted out gym, the chance to play sports for your college and the UWA Aquatic Centre offering swimming lessons, competition training, aquatics sports and events. There are also cafes, shops, pharmacies and more essential shops around campus for easy access.</p>",
