    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Western Australia (UWA) is a public research university situated in Perth, Western Australia. Founded in 1911, it is one of the most prestigious universities in Australia.</p><p>Recognised internationally for its exceptional learning, research and faculties, it is also one of the oldest universities in Australia. UWA holds a five-star rating for teaching quality, facilitating meaningful teaching, learning and research in the Good Universities Guide, so graduates from this acknowledged university have the best possible chance of future success.</p><p>Other notable amenities include the UWA Aquatic Centre or the John de Laeter Centre for Mass Spectrometry.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The University of Western Australia has a variety of accommodation options for students. UWA houses 5 residential colleges that are located just opposite the main campus and a short walk from all other areas of the university. Colloquially called College Row, students benefit from wi-fi, a community feel, modern amenities, all meals included and a high quality of life.</p><p>UWA is partnered with MyStay International and Australian Homestay Network (AHN) to offer UWA Hosted Accommodation with a local Perth family. AHN provides host background checks, airport transfers, 24/7 professionally staffed emergency support, and much more. Students might also choose to live off-campus or in the city of Perth with friends or family members.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>Students can be assured of the quality of the facilities at this prestigious university, with sports facilities so students can stay active such as the UWA Sports Park.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>UWA houses first-rate lecture theaters, laboratories and places of learning like the Reid and Science libraries that are packed with information for students to enjoy.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>More than 25,000 students find a home on the main campus, with more than 4,000 international students coming from 100 countries to study here.</p><p>There are over 160 student clubs and societies to join, including Australia's most active Student Guild for students who want to make their voice heard. UWA sport opportunities are surplus, with a fully kitted out gym, the chance to play sports for your college and the UWA Aquatic Centre offering swimming lessons, competition training, aquatics sports and events. There are also cafes, shops, pharmacies and more essential shops around campus for easy access.</p>",
